{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Seek from upon the scroll of YHWH.</b> An allusion to the decrees of heaven, which are written by the finger of Elohim. The meaning is that all the decrees shall come upon the land of Edom, including those inscribed to be — that the land of Edom shall be a haunt for them:" "<b>For the mouth.</b> An allusion to the decrees that go forth from the mouth of HaShem:" "<b>And His spirit.</b> The spirit of His mouth. And behold, the meaning is doubled, as is the rule:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:42.331930994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}